        ("Roof tile and the eave line", "Barrel and flat tile leave hollow channels at the ridge and along the eaves. A colony can build comb in that space for months before anyone notices more than a steady line of bees at one corner of the roof. Our [[svc:roofs|tile roof hive]] page covers the lift-and-reset work."),
